# Software for Classroom Music Making.

**Authors:** Ely, Mark C.

## Abstract
Describes musical instrument digital interface (MIDI), a communication system that uses digital data to enable MIDI-equipped instruments to communicate with each other. Includes discussion of music editors, sequencers, compositional software, and commonly used computers. Suggests uses for the technology for students and teachers. Urges further exploration of possible teaching applications. (DK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ452260

